      "area": "Actual unsupported mount",
      "status": "source_checked",
      "detail": "Both root and plain namespace engine profiles admit root SSH but reject Backend::Kubernetes. The existing native KV2 mount creation fallback rejects any non-KV2 type with 501; the two negative mount assertions retain their original ACL/CAS/graph context."
    },
    {
      "area": "Actual unsupported private owner",
      "status": "source_checked",
      "detail": "The fixture uses real internal EC-256 PKI key generation. LocalPrivateMaterial::generate is published into RootCa.local_material; RootCa and Pki serialize this private material. Configuring the local cluster URL satisfies the enabled-ACME write precondition. enabled=true is nondefault AcmeConfig, making Pki::native_local_profile false. No ACME account/order/challenge/provider operation is added."
    },
    {
      "area": "Configured File refusal",
      "status": "source_checked",
      "detail": "409 and native_root absence remain. The added before/after engine-byte comparison uses Zeroizing buffers with native_root absent, after successful V5 key/config writes; it does not flatten a live native KV view. The original public configuration equality is preserved."
    },
    {
      "area": "Cold archive refusal and source retention",
      "status": "byte_checked",
      "detail": "Both protected route 501 checks, exact ColdSeedError::GraphRejected, destination absence, generation and StateIdentity equality, complete ALL-State/opaque-engine/authenticated-KV projection, archive bytes, seal bytes and Shamir digest assertions remain. The complete projection and recovery/source-retention blocks are byte-identical. The actual cold-seed root_scope calls native_plain::profile and returns GraphRejected before seed publication."
    },
    {
      "area": "Rust and deadlines",
      "status": "static_checked",
      "detail": "No concrete new import, Value ownership or mutable/immutable borrow conflict was found. Array tuples move their JSON Values into existing request APIs; V5 engine borrows end before the next mutable request. All original deadline/timeout expression lines in the four files match exactly. This is not a compiler or runtime result."
